      <activity id="9a957682-1e5b-5208-8ff5-e82f33a60f1e" activityNameId="1290d3eb-d280-5b60-90bb-0a2910797e3f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, exhaust air valve, in-wall housing, plastic/steel, DN 125</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, exhaust air valve, in-wall housing, plastic/steel, DN 125
Disposal of an exhaust air outlet mounted in room ceiling. Including housing for duct connection. component made of polyvinylchloride and zinc coated steel. Compatible with ducts of 40-120 cm2 section area. Weight per element 0.5 kg;
UUID: 6351410c-7338-42b0-9083-de371b2f361a
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces and copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Questionnaire and assumptions. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6351410c-7338-42b0-9083-de371b2f361a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
